WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.922
In this video you will make your own OurWater
account.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:09.154
We fill in the form one box at a time, then
finish with the code from your email.

00:00:09.274 --> 00:00:12.202
It is free, and it takes about a minute.

00:00:13.017 --> 00:00:17.169
You see this page when you open OurWater and
are not signed in.

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:20.409
If you are new, tap Create a free account.

00:00:21.217 --> 00:00:23.881
This is the form that makes your account.

00:00:24.001 --> 00:00:26.929
It is free, and it takes about a minute.

00:00:27.049 --> 00:00:29.689
We fill it in one box at a time.

00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:34.765
To read the page in another language, tap this
button at the top.

00:00:35.583 --> 00:00:37.671
First, your name.

00:00:37.791 --> 00:00:40.911
This is only how OurWater speaks to you.

00:00:41.031 --> 00:00:43.719
A first name or a nickname is fine.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.118
Next, your email address.

00:00:47.238 --> 00:00:51.174
We send one code here, to check that it is
really you.

00:00:51.294 --> 00:00:54.006
Use an address you can open today.

00:00:54.817 --> 00:00:56.809
Now choose a username.

00:00:56.929 --> 00:00:58.945
You can sign in with it.

00:00:59.065 --> 00:01:05.929
It needs at least eight characters: small letters,
numbers, dots, underscores or hyphens.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.886
Next, your country.

00:01:09.006 --> 00:01:13.278
A username only has to be different from the
others in the same country,

00:01:13.398 --> 00:01:16.278
so the name check needs to know where you
live.

00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:18.955
Now type a name.

00:01:19.075 --> 00:01:21.547
OurWater checks it as you type.

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:25.339
A red line means someone in your country
already has it.

00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:28.339
Below, you get three free names.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.022
Watch the username.

00:01:31.142 --> 00:01:35.414
This name was taken in India, but it is free
in Australia.

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:38.078
Green means it is yours to use.

00:01:38.883 --> 00:01:42.003
Back to India, and it is taken again.

00:01:42.123 --> 00:01:45.507
So always choose the country where you really
live.

00:01:46.317 --> 00:01:49.869
Tap one of the free names, and it fills the
box.

00:01:49.989 --> 00:01:51.933
The line turns green.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.910
Or type a name of your own.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.902
I will keep this one.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.901
Choose your preferred language.

00:02:00.021 --> 00:02:02.469
There are more than sixty to pick from.

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:06.069
The app works without internet once it has
downloaded.

00:02:06.883 --> 00:02:08.755
Now a password.

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:14.971
Use at least eight characters, with a big
letter, a small letter, a number and a symbol.

00:02:15.091 --> 00:02:17.107
The grey line reminds you.

00:02:17.917 --> 00:02:20.629
Tap the little eye to see what you typed.

00:02:20.749 --> 00:02:22.765
It helps most on a phone.

00:02:22.885 --> 00:02:24.901
Tap it again to hide it.

00:02:25.717 --> 00:02:28.045
Type the same password again.

00:02:28.165 --> 00:02:31.333
If they do not match, a red line tells you.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:36.086
Next, the Terms and Conditions and the Privacy
Policy.

00:02:36.206 --> 00:02:40.334
Each link opens in a new tab, so you keep your
place here.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.310
Tick the box when you agree.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:48.590
It also says that other OurWater users can see
the measurements and stations you add.

00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:51.817
The second box is about age.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:54.889
Tick it to say you are eighteen or older.

00:02:55.009 --> 00:02:59.857
If you are younger, ask your school or
organisation to make an account for you.

00:03:00.683 --> 00:03:02.555
Every box is filled.

00:03:02.675 --> 00:03:04.547
Tap Create account.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:10.318
OurWater sends a six-digit code to your email,
and opens this page.

00:03:10.438 --> 00:03:13.174
Your account is waiting for that code.

00:03:13.983 --> 00:03:16.359
This box shows your username.

00:03:16.479 --> 00:03:19.263
You can change it later from your profile.

00:03:20.083 --> 00:03:22.627
Check that the email address is right.

00:03:22.747 --> 00:03:24.643
The code was sent here.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:29.410
If it is wrong, tap Register again, and start
over.

00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:35.665
Open your email, find the message from
OurWater, and type the six numbers here.

00:03:35.785 --> 00:03:37.705
Then tap Verify.

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:41.829
If a number is wrong, you see a red message.

00:03:41.949 --> 00:03:44.397
Check the numbers and try again.

00:03:44.517 --> 00:03:48.021
After five wrong tries, ask for a new code.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.266
No message?

00:03:50.386 --> 00:03:54.082
Wait a minute, then look in your junk or spam
folder.

00:03:54.202 --> 00:03:57.178
Mail from a new sender often goes there.

00:03:57.983 --> 00:03:59.855
Still nothing?

00:03:59.975 --> 00:04:01.871
Tap Resend code.

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:05.591
You get a new code, and the old one stops
working.

00:04:06.417 --> 00:04:10.065
When the code is right, you come to this
sign-in page.

00:04:10.185 --> 00:04:14.481
Sign in with your email or your username, and
your password.

00:04:15.283 --> 00:04:18.907
If you forget your password one day, use this
link.

00:04:19.027 --> 00:04:22.531
We send a code, and you choose a new password.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:25.222
That is all.

00:04:25.342 --> 00:04:28.702
Check your email for the code, then sign in.

00:04:28.822 --> 00:04:35.014
A new account starts as a Data Contributor, so you
can add your own stations and record measurements.

00:04:35.134 --> 00:04:38.014
Thank you for helping look after our water.
